GNU-style NEWS file for crabbucket.  User-visible changes, newest first.

* Noteworthy changes in release 0.1.0 (unreleased) [alpha]

** New features

  Initial import.  A site is Markdown content with `+++' TOML frontmatter
  and a `site.toml'; `crab build' renders it to a directory of static
  pages, one directory per route.

  Design tokens are generated from design/tokens.toml into both Rust
  constants and CSS custom properties, so the two cannot drift apart.

  The base path is recorded once and applied in one place, so a project
  site served from /repo/ works without any page knowing about it.

  Layouts are an associated type on the theme.  `layout = "docs"'
  deserializes into the theme's own enum, so a layout that does not exist
  fails the build listing the ones that do.

  Every internal link is resolved after rendering and checked against the
  routes and assets the build produced.  A dead link fails the build,
  with every offender listed at once, each naming the page that wrote it.
  There is no flag to disable it.

  An optional client-side router of about a kilobyte swaps <main> and
  drives the View Transitions API, and degrades to ordinary navigation.

** Notes

  The design is described in doc/DESIGN.  What is planned, and why, is in
  ROADMAP.md and in cairn/items.

  Still unbuilt, and described as such: a generated Route enum, Markdown
  directives, heading ids, syntax highlighting and search.

  There is no dev server, and there will not be one.  Run `turborust up'.
